 "note": {
  "status": "draft",
  "text": "A biography is the story of a person's life written by someone else. It usually follows time order: birth and childhood, education, career, achievements, and sometimes death.\nIt uses the simple past and time words.\n\nText: Two lives in art\nManu Dibango was born in Douala in 1933. As a young man he went to study in France, where he learnt the saxophone and the piano. In 1972 his song “Soul Makossa” became a world hit and made makossa famous. He was called “Papa Groove”. He died in 2020.\nAdah Mbeng (a model biography written for this lesson) grew up in Bamenda. She loved acting in school plays. After secondary school she joined a theatre group, then acted in short films. Her first feature film won a prize in Yaoundé. Today she trains young actors: “Talent is a seed; work is the rain.”",
  "checks": []
 },
